  "solution": {
    "approach": "The program initializes two integers a = 5 and b = 10. It then swaps their values using a temporary variable (or tuple assignment) and prints the swapped values. Since there is no input, the same output is produced for every execution.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) per execution.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) – only a few integer variables are used.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        // No input needed for this problem\n        int a = 5, b = 10;\n        int temp = a;\n        a = b;\n        b = temp;\n        System.out.print(a + \" \" + b);\n    }\n}",
